 ],
 "notes": "Luz Ardiden from Luz-Saint-Sauveur (app: start 721 m, 13.1 km, Sazos km 2.7, Grust km 4.3). km 0 = the junction in Saint-Sauveur where the D12 Route de l'Ardiden leaves the D921 (Avenue de l'Impératrice Eugénie), ~1.2 km from Luz centre; the app profile fits this foot best (DEM 712 m, per-km rms 0.6 %). Route: D12 only — hairpins below Sazos, Sazos, Grust, the forest section with hairpin pairs, out of the forest at ~km 9, then the open hairpin stack up to the station; finish at the end of the road at the ski station car park. Coordinates are on the Overture/OSM road geometry; km are routed distances from the foot (routed 13.21 km vs 13.1 km, +0.9 %). The Tour 2021 (stage 18) itinerary gives a 13.3 km final climb starting about 1.1 km after the Saint-Sauveur thermal station, i.e. roughly at this junction; its Sazos/Grust km are not consistent with the map (Sazos lies ~120 m above the road), so the village km here are the routed positions. The exact finish-line spot (end of a 130 m final straight at the station) is taken as the end of the D12 at the car park (DEM ~1712 m).",
